  "prompt": "26 October 2025 was the day the clocks went back in Europe. For each user with activation events on that UTC day, count their activation sessions that day, using only that day's events, so each user's first event of the day starts a session. A user's first activation event starts a session, and an event more than 30 minutes after the same user's previous event starts a new one; an event exactly 30 minutes later stays in the same session. Measure each gap as the time between the two moments in event_ts, a UTC instant. When two events of a user share a moment, take them in event_name order, A to Z. Return two columns, in this order: user_id and sessions. Return one row for each user with events that day. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "user_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "sessions",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      }
    ],
    "grain": null
  },
